# serial_cycle_wide_wired -- the same ring of four, with one bare channel
# across it, and the reason disjoint memory is not the whole question.
#
# serial_cycle_wide gives `alder` and `cedar` no region in common, which is
# what lets them run at the same moment: neither can see a byte the other
# writes. This declaration keeps every region and every grant exactly as
# that document has them, and adds one line -- `channel alder cedar`.
#
# Nothing about the memory changed. The flows are the same four one-way
# streets, the shape still reads as a ring, and `share_a_region` still
# answers no for that pair. What changed is that alder and cedar now hold a
# doorbell between them, and a doorbell is state: one side rings it, the
# other hears it and clears it, and two dependents racing on one counter is
# the same hazard a shared region carries, one layer up.
#
# So this document exists to state a boundary. Channels are declared apart
# from grants, so a document may wire two domains that share no memory at
# all, and a concurrency test that read only the grants would wave this
# pair through. Two domains may run at once when they share no region *and*
# no channel; either alone is a half-answer.
#
# Read whole by `caravan/read.rye`; refused for that pair by
# `caravan/concurrent.rye`.

system serial_cycle_wide_wired

domain alder
domain birch
domain cedar
domain dogwood

channel alder birch
channel birch cedar
channel cedar dogwood
channel dogwood alder
channel alder cedar

region ask_ab 4096
region ask_bc 4096
region ask_cd 4096
region ask_da 4096
region taken 64

grant ask_ab alder rw
grant ask_ab birch r
grant ask_bc birch rw
grant ask_bc cedar r
grant ask_cd cedar rw
grant ask_cd dogwood r
grant ask_da dogwood rw
grant ask_da alder r
grant taken alder rw
grant taken dogwood r
